' Sequence Diagram 02 — Frontier resolution: warm up-walk vs cold down-walk.
'
' parent_frontier(parent, J) resolves the highest witnessed-finalized block on
' the parent's main spine. It has two paths:
'   - WARM (incremental_frontier): cache-hit pivot F(parent) + two guards +
'     an amortized-O(1) up-walk that calls the oracle ONLY while advancing.
'   - COLD (cold_parent_frontier): the original top-down walk, one oracle call
'     per step, taken on cache miss / guard trip / off-spine / genesis.
' T-CACHE: both paths yield the identical frontier (Floor.frontier_cache_transparent).
'
' Source of truth for the "determinism linchpin" figure in
' docs/theory/finalized-floor/finalized-floor-verification.md (section 3.1).
'
' Render:
'   plantuml -tsvg docs/theory/finalized-floor/diagrams/02-seq-warm-vs-cold-walk.puml

@startuml 02-seq-warm-vs-cold-walk
!theme plain

title Frontier resolution ── warm up-walk vs cold down-walk (T-CACHE: warm == cold)

skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor              #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor     #666666
  ParticipantBorderColor  #333333
  NoteBorderColor         #666666
  NoteBackgroundColor     #FFF8E1
  GroupBorderColor        #333333
  GroupHeaderFontColor    #222222
  DividerBackgroundColor  #ECEFF1
}
skinparam defaultFontName "monospace"
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

autonumber

participant "derive_floor\n(casper/…/finality/floor.rs)"        as DF #B2DFDB
database    "FrontierCache\n(LMDB frontier_index)"               as FC #D7CCC8
participant "CliqueOracle\nft_witnessed > θ"                     as OR #FFECB3

note over DF, OR #ECEFF1
  GOAL — parent_frontier(parent, J), J = just(child) ⊇ just(parent):
  the highest main-spine ancestor of `parent` that is finalized over J.

  COLOR LEGEND
  blue (#1565C0) = read query    ·  purple (#6A1B9A) = oracle call (ft_witnessed)
  green (#2E7D32) = finalized/ok  ·  orange (#E65100) = advance / stop verdict
  gray (#546E7A) = cheap local hop (no oracle)  ·  red (#C62828) = guard trip → fallback
end note

alt #E8F5E9 WARM path — cache hit and both guards hold

  DF -[#1565C0]> FC ++ : read cached pivot F(parent)
  FC -[#2E7D32]-> DF -- : pivot p := F(parent)  (finalized over just(parent))

  DF -[#546E7A]> DF : committee-constancy guard\nget_corresponding_weight_map across band\n(cheap metadata — NO oracle call)
  note right of DF #E8F5E9
    L-ANC premise: committee constant ⟹ finalized
    blocks are a downward-closed spine prefix.
    (GuardBridge.chain_adj_AdjDC)
  end note

  DF -[#6A1B9A]> OR ++ : L-SNAP guard — ft_witnessed(p) > θ\nover the LARGER snapshot J ?
  OR -[#2E7D32]-> DF -- : yes — pivot still finalized  (L-SNAP)

  loop up-walk from pivot toward parent — amortized O(1)
    DF -[#546E7A]> DF : main_parent hop  b := advance(b)\n(cheap spine hop — NO oracle)
    DF -[#6A1B9A]> OR ++ : ft_witnessed(b) > θ ?   [ONLY while advancing]
    OR -[#E65100]-> DF -- : finalized ⟹ advance · not finalized ⟹ STOP
  end
  DF -[#E65100]> DF : stop at first non-finalized\n⟹ frontier := highest finalized

else #FFEBEE COLD path — cache miss / guard trip / off-spine / genesis

  DF -[#1565C0]> FC ++ : read F(parent)
  FC -[#C62828]-> DF -- : MISS  (or a warm guard tripped above)
  loop top-down from parent down to first finalized (or genesis)
    DF -[#6A1B9A]> OR ++ : ft_witnessed(step) > θ ?   [one call per step DOWN]
    OR -[#E65100]-> DF -- : not finalized ⟹ step down · finalized ⟹ STOP
  end
  DF -[#E65100]> DF : first finalized from the top\n⟹ frontier := highest finalized

end

note over DF, OR #FFF8E1
  T-CACHE (the determinism linchpin).
  By L-ANC (constant committee) finalized blocks are a DOWNWARD-CLOSED
  PREFIX of the spine ⟹ warm result == cold result
  (Rocq Floor.frontier_cache_transparent; GuardBridge.chain_adj_AdjDC derives
  the AdjDC premise from the committee-constancy guard). The cache never forks (S1).
end note

@enduml
